Callable after find_tools:
- list_customers — List customers narrowed by status, code, name or city, with their ids.
- list_billing_queue_items — List billing queue items, the shipments waiting on a biller.
- get_billing_queue_item — Open one billing queue item with its payer, shipment and the charges this payer is billed.
- get_billing_queue_items — Open several billing queue items by id in one call, each with what blocks its approval and what its shipment still lacks for billing.
- assign_billing_queue_billers — Assign one biller to several billing queue items in one call, so the person decides it once.
- transition_items_to_in_review — Move several billing queue items into review in one call, so the person decides it once.
- hold_billing_queue_item — Put a billing queue item on hold, with a note saying what it waits on.
- move_billing_item_to_exception — Move a billing queue item in review into exception for a biller to resolve.
- send_billing_item_back_to_ops — Send a billing queue item in review back to operations to fix, with a reason.
- approve_billing_queue_item — Propose approving a billing queue item you have reviewed and found clean.
- approve_billing_queue_items — Propose approving several billing queue items you have reviewed and found clean, in one proposal the person approves together.
- cancel_billing_queue_item — Propose canceling a billing queue item that should never be billed, such as a duplicate of another item.
- list_invoices — List invoices narrowed by status, whether they are paid, whether they are disputed, the amount, or the invoice and due dates.
- get_invoice — Retrieve one invoice by id, with its line items, totals, payment and dispute state.
- get_invoices — Retrieve several invoices by id in one call, each with its status, totals, payment state and line items.
- post_invoice — Propose posting a draft invoice, usually the one approve_billing_queue_item just made.
- send_invoice — Propose emailing an invoice to the customer.
- post_invoices — Propose posting several draft invoices in one proposal the person approves together.
- send_invoices — Propose emailing several invoices to their customers in one proposal the person approves together.
- list_reports — List the reports this organization can run and what each takes: built-in ones with a reportKey, and ones saved in the report builder with a definitionId.
- describe_report — Show what a report contains: its dataset, columns, filters, sort, parameters and the full definition as the report builder saves it.
- run_report — Start one of the reports from list_reports: a built-in one by reportKey or a saved one by definitionId, whichever dataset it reads.
- list_email_profiles — The sending profiles email can go out from: each has a name, a sender address and a reply-to.
- request_missing_docs — Request missing documentation from a party by sending them an email.
- list_accessorial_charges — List the accessorial charges this organization bills — detention, layover, lumper and the rest — with how each is calculated and at what rate.
- add_shipment_comment — Leave a note on a shipment's comment thread, where dispatch will read it.
- update_invoice_draft — Change what a draft invoice says and where it goes: its memo, remittance instructions, email subject and body, recipients and attached documents.
- generate_invoice_pdf — Render an invoice's PDF from what it says now and file it on the invoice, replacing the one there.
- void_invoice — Propose voiding an invoice.
- create_invoice_memo — Propose a draft credit or debit memo to a customer with no shipment behind it, such as a goodwill credit or a returned-check fee.
- send_invoice_edi — Propose sending a posted invoice to the customer's EDI partner as a 210.
- search_documents — Search the text of documents: rate confirmations, bills of lading, proofs of delivery, invoices, contracts, permits and other files attached to records.
- list_invoice_adjustments — List the invoice adjustments on one invoice, drafts included, or those waiting for an approver.
- get_invoice_adjustment — Retrieve one invoice adjustment by id: its kind, status, approval, reason, the invoices it made and each line it credits or rebills against the invoice's lines.
- save_invoice_adjustment_draft — Save a draft credit, rebill, reversal or write-off on a posted invoice for a biller to review and submit; nothing is credited until it is submitted.
- submit_invoice_adjustment — Propose crediting, rebilling, reversing or writing off posted invoices.
- approve_invoice_adjustment — Propose approving an invoice adjustment that waits for approval, which executes it: the credit memo and any replacement invoice are made and posted.
- reject_invoice_adjustment — Propose rejecting an invoice adjustment that waits for approval, with the reason the submitter will read.
- list_invoice_runs — List invoice runs, the reviewable batches of consolidated invoices for a billing period, by status, number or period.
- get_invoice_run — Retrieve one invoice run by id with each group, the invoice it would make or made, and the items in it: the ids adjust_invoice_run_membership moves or excludes.
- build_invoice_run — Build an invoice run: a reviewable proposal of the consolidated invoices for customers' approved, uninvoiced freight over a period.
- commit_invoice_run — Propose committing an invoice run, which turns each of its proposed invoices into a draft invoice for the customer.
- cancel_invoice_run — Cancel an invoice run that will never be committed, such as one built for the wrong period or customers.
- bill_statement_now — Propose billing a statement customer's open period now, before its cycle closes, with the reason recorded on the run.
- list_invoice_share_candidates — List the teammates an invoice can be shared with: only people whose role lets them read invoices.
- share_invoice — Propose sharing an invoice with teammates, who get a notification and an email with your note and a link to it.
- reassign_billing_charge — Move who pays one charge on a shipment in billing review: its freight or one accessorial, whole to another payer or split among several.
- manage_billing_transfer_run — Stop a background transfer to billing that is still running, or Retry the shipments a finished one could not transfer.

Several records in one call: get_billing_queue_items does get_billing_queue_item for a list, assign_billing_queue_billers does assign_billing_queue_biller for a list, transition_items_to_in_review does transition_item_to_in_review for a list, approve_billing_queue_items does approve_billing_queue_item for a list, get_invoices does get_invoice for a list, post_invoices does post_invoice for a list, send_invoices does send_invoice for a list. When the person asks about several records, or for one change across several, call the list tool once with all of them, so a change is decided once on one card; never call the single tool once per record, and load the list tool with find_tools when it is not loaded.

How a task is done with these, in order, each step's result feeding the next; skip a step whose answer you already have:
- transfer_to_billing: list_billing_transfer_candidates → transfer_to_billing
- assign_billing_queue_billers: list_billing_queue_items → get_billing_queue_items → assign_billing_queue_billers
- approve_billing_queue_items: list_billing_queue_items → get_billing_queue_items → assign_billing_queue_billers → approve_billing_queue_items → post_invoices
- post_invoices: approve_billing_queue_items → post_invoices → send_invoices
- run_report: list_reports → describe_report → run_report
- submit_invoice_adjustment: get_invoice → save_invoice_adjustment_draft → submit_invoice_adjustment
- build_invoice_run: list_open_statements → build_invoice_run → get_invoice_run → commit_invoice_run
- share_invoice: list_invoice_share_candidates → share_invoice
